## failures found while writing the tests and fixed in the runner (no skip/xfail):
- test_connection_refused_is_a_failure: a refused connection reported connected=True (the 'other tenant cannot read' check is true without a server) -> connected now requires a real answer (write accepted / row read)
- test_secrets_never_reach_report_stdout_or_logs_even_on_exceptions: an unexpected exception inside a probe crashed the runner with a traceback carrying the secret value -> run_target turns it into FAIL 'probe error: <type>' and main() has a redacted last-resort handler
- test_fully_enabled_live_endpoint_still_must_resolve_publicly (test assumption): under the conftest fake DNS (TEST-NET treated as public by the suite) the live probe reaches the offline guard -> split into a DNS-refusal test (BLOCKED) and a no-network live test (FAIL, connected=False, never PASS)
- workflow static test: the header comment contained the word 'secrets.' -> reworded
- three timeout/cancel tests took 30 s each because the fakes' hang handlers blocked server shutdown -> fake hang 4 s (probe deadline 1 s)
